	(text "HOUSEKEEPING RAIL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.7200 81.2800 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8000 1.8000)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7fe338b3-3475-d8ab-6dec-8e2bd4b26207")
	)
	(text_box "ONE SHARED RAIL FOR EVERY THRESHOLD-SETTING GATE.\n+3V3_A feeds all 14 squarers, all 26 flip-flops, all 12 Schmitts and the whole\nhelper fan-out.  A gate's switching threshold moves with its supply, so on a\nshared rail every channel's threshold moves TOGETHER - common mode, and it\ncancels in the differences we actually compute.  Fourteen separate regulators\nwould make fourteen thresholds wander independently and turn a cancelling error\ninto one that does not."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.2400 144.7800 0)
		(size 121.9200 21.5900)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "48aab62d-abc5-d1f0-994a-b701352119c0")
	)
	(text_box "WHY A SECOND RAIL AT ALL.\n+3V3_D carries only the Si5351, the TCXO and the I2C housekeeping parts.  None\nof them sets a comparison threshold, and they draw the lumpiest current on the\nboard. Splitting them off halves the dissipation in each SOT-23 package - about\n120 mW and 50 mW instead of 170 mW in one - which matters on a board whose whole\npurpose is thermal stability."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.7800 144.7800 0)
		(size 121.9200 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e23bbb6a-2368-e9bd-ea8a-21592438cb0e")
	)
	(text_box "WHY THE TPS7A2033.\n3.8 uV RMS output noise, 300 mA, and 52 000 in stock at JLCPCB.  The obvious\nalternative, the ADP151, is 9 uV and 200 mA and is not stocked there at all -\nonly re-marked house-brand parts are.  The 10 nF on NR/SS is what buys the low\nnoise figure; without it the part is ordinary."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 274.3200 144.7800 0)
		(size 121.9200 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b5f1b260-b139-1066-f236-f19bf2712194")
	)
	(text_box "STUDENT-PROOFING THE 5 V INPUT.\nBench supplies get set wrong.  Three things, in order: each source has its own\nSERIES SCHOTTKY, so reversed leads conduct nothing and the two sources cannot\nback-feed each other; a 500 mA PPTC, which RESETS ITSELF - nobody has to find\nthe bag of spare fuses; and a 5.6 V 5 W Zener, which is the part that saves the\nboard if 12 V lands on the 5 V posts.\nThe Zener is what makes the fuse work: it clamps the rail near 6.1 V - under the\nTPS7A2033's 6.5 V absolute maximum - and draws the amp that trips the PPTC in\nabout 100 ms.  It is the deliberate sacrificial part, and it is a 16-cent SMB on\nthe board edge.\nWhat is NOT protected: sustained reverse voltage beyond the SS34's 40 V, and\nanything applied directly to an SMA or the header pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 403.8600 144.7800 0)
		(size 121.9200 34.2900)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 220 220 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4d7aff61-16b4-1185-e638-00e6398518ed")
	)
	(text_box "CURRENT BUDGET, ~100 mA TOTAL.\n14 x 74LVC1GU04 self-biased in the linear region ~3 mA each = 42 mA;  26 x\n74LVC1G80 at 10 MHz ~1 mA each = 26 mA;  5 x 74LVC1G34 fan-out ~2 mA each = 10\nmA; 12 x 74LVC1G17 at 1 Hz ~ 1 mA total;  Si5351 ~25 mA.  The linear-region\ncurrent of a self-biased unbuffered inverter is not a datasheet number - measure\nit on the first board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 403.8600 100.3300 0)
		(size 121.9200 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "888ec856-14a2-5a6d-ccc1-fda10aa48e28")
	)
